Fixed and committed as 4c981de1, closing #1195. config get and config show now show the value the run actually uses whenever it differs from what's written in the file. Before this they only flagged values read as "unset". The checks all passed: cargo build, cargo test (no failures), clippy -D warnings and fmt --check.

Output from the built binary (run with a temporary home and working directory; before and after tables are posted on #1195):

| .yoyo.toml | yoyo config get before | after |
|---|---|---|
| thinking = "" | thinking =   (.yoyo.toml) | … (read as medium) |
| thinking = "max" | thinking = max | … (read as high) |
| temperature = 5 | temperature = 5 | … (read as 1.0) |
| provider = "bogus" / "github" | shown as written | … (read as an unknown / a retired provider; startup refuses it unless a base URL is given) |
| max_auto_continues = 50 | = 50 | … (read as 20) |

config show gets the same notes, and config get prints no warnings to stderr. I ran yoyo -p hi with each of those two providers to confirm startup really refuses them.

What changed:
• `src/cli.rs` (+17 lines, within the size limit): I split out two warning-free helpers, thinking_level_from_str and clamped_temperature. The existing parse_thinking_level and clamp_temperature now call them, so the run and config get read values with the same code.
• `src/commands_config_get.rs`: the old run_reads_as_unset -> Option<bool> had provider and thinking hardcoded to "fine". It's replaced by run_reading -> Option<RunReading { AsWritten, Unset, As(String) }>, so there's now a slot for "the run uses a third value". unset_reading_note returns a String, and the call site in commands_config.rs compiles without edits.
• Tests: a new test goes through every key in SETTABLE_KEYS with an unusual value, and every key needs a row; none are exempt. It turned up two cases the ticket didn't list: max_auto_continues is capped at 20, and booleans written as yes/1/on are now shown as (read as true). There are also explicit rows for the ticket's thinking, temperature and provider cases. When I broke the provider reading on purpose, both new tests failed by name; after restoring it they pass.
• Docs: I added one sentence to docs/src/getting-started/installation.md, where config get's "read as unset" behaviour was already described. That's a file outside the task's list.

One problem I didn't fix: /config set temperature 1.5 is accepted, because validation allows 0.0–2.0 and the key's description says the same. The run then clamps it to 1.0. Since this push closes #1195, I filed it separately as #1204. I found it by reading the code and haven't tested it in a live session.
